+3.  **Calculate Surface Orientation:**
+    For a specific block at grid position $(x, y, z)$, compute its world-space vertical bounds:
+    $$ Z_{bottom} = z \cdot B $$
+    $$ Z_{top} = (z + 1) \cdot B $$
+    Determine the vertical orientation relative to the camera:
+    $$ \text{orientation} = \begin{cases} 1 & \text{if } P_z < Z_{bottom} \quad (\text{Camera below block}) \\ 2 & \text{if } P_z > Z_{top} \quad (\text{Camera above block}) \\ 0 & \text{otherwise} \quad (\text{Camera inside or level with block}) \end{cases} $$
+    [S2, unofficial]
 
-3. **Calculate Block Geometry and Orientation:**
-   For a block at grid coordinates $(x, y, z)$ within a chunk:
-   $$
-   \begin{aligned}
-   B_x &= chunkX + x \cdot BLOCK\_SIZE \\
-   B_y &= chunkY + y \cdot BLOCK\_SIZE \\
-   B_{z,bot} &= chunkZ + z \cdot BLOCK\_SIZE \\
-   B_{z,top} &= B_{z,bot} + BLOCK\_SIZE
-   \end{aligned}
-   $$
-   [S1, unofficial]
-   
-   Determine surface orientation relative to the camera's vertical position:
-   $$
-   \text{orientation} = 
-   \begin{cases} 
-   1 & \text{if } P_z < B_{z,bot} \quad (\text{Looking up}) \\
-   2 & \text{if } P_z > B_{z,top} \quad (\text{Looking down}) \\
-   0 & \text{otherwise} \quad (\text{Level view})
-   \end{cases}
-   $$
-   [S1, unofficial]
